      "previewText": "The following is a second-order reaction.If k = @@k@@ M-1 min-1 and the initial concentration of A is 0.850 M, how long will it take for the concentration of A to be @@concFinal@@ M?t =  minAt a different temperature, k = @@k2@@ M-1 min-1. If the initial concentration of A is 0.750 M, what will the concentration of A be after @@time@@ min?[A]t =  M",
      "targeted": [],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "children": [],
          "data": [
            {
              "children": [],
              "expression": "// Two variable definitions\nconst k = OLI.random(0.00222, 0.00888, 6) .toFixed(5);\nconst concIndex = OLI.random (0,5);\nconst array = [0.650,0.550,0.450,0.350,0.250,0.150];\nconst concFinal = array[concIndex] .toFixed(3);\nconst concFinalInv = (1/concFinal) .toPrecision(3);\nconst concInvMin = (concFinalInv-1.176);\nconst correct = (concInvMin/k);\nconst correctRounded = (concInvMin/k) .toPrecision(3);\nconst corLow = correct*0.98;\nconst corHigh = correct*1.02;\nconst k2 = OLI.random(0.400,1.40,3) .toPrecision(3);\nconst time = OLI.random(0.400,1.50,3) .toPrecision(3);\nconst step1 = ((k2*time)+1.3333);\nconst invRound = step1 .toPrecision(3);\nconst correct2 = (1/step1);\nconst cor2Round = correct2 .toPrecision(3);\nconst cor2Low = correct2*0.98;\nconst cor2High = correct2*1.02;\n\n// Expose variables to OLI\nmodule.exports = {\n k,\n concIndex,\n array,\n concFinal,\n concFinalInv,\n concInvMin,\n correct,\n correctRounded,\n corLow,\n corHigh,\n k2,\n time,\n step1,\n invRound,\n correct2,\n cor2Round,\n cor2Low,\n cor2High\n};\n",
